In this paper, we study the Hyers-Ulam stability of the following equation \begin{multline*}
  ϕ(x+y-z)+ϕ(x+z-y)+ϕ(y+z-x)=ϕ(x-y)+ϕ(x-z)+ϕ(z-y)
  +ϕ(x)+ϕ(y) +ϕ(z) \end{multline*}
  in modular space, with or without $Δ_2$-condition, and in $β$-homogeneous Banach space.

